# Project Description

This project is part of the UniTime timetable management system.

The selected subsystem is the Security Rights subsystem. It controls user permissions for different parts of the system such as courses, events, and rooms.

The original issue is that all permissions were grouped in one large enum called Right.java, which made the code hard to maintain and understand.

The required change is to organize related permissions into separate enums:
- CourseRight
- EventRight
- RoomRight

This improves readability, maintainability, and separation of concerns.
